{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe over-optimism: The model consistently forecasts a linear upward trajectory or plateau near 95-100 EUR, failing to anticipate the sharp crash (mean reversion) to the 65-70 EUR range that occurs 5-10 days after price spikes above 90 EUR.",
    "Apply aggressive downward correction after positive sentiment spikes: When sentiment history shows values > 0.30 (e.g., 0.33, 0.40, 0.60) coinciding with price spikes, the model's forecast is systematically too high by 15-25 EUR; reduce forecasts immediately to reflect the high probability of a reversal.",
    "Eliminate momentum bias: The model exhibits a 'momentum trap' where it extrapolates recent gains indefinitely; apply a mean-reversion heuristic that forces forecasts to decline once the 30-day horizon extends beyond the immediate next 3-4 days following a peak.",
    "Adjust for lag in volatility recognition: The model fails to react to the volatility regime shift (from ~90 EUR to ~70 EUR) until the drop has already occurred; forecasts should be adjusted downward by 20% of the recent 5-day price drop magnitude immediately upon detecting a break below the 90 EUR support level."
  ]
}
